		"description": "<p>(INT/Safe Rest) When you hit a creature with a thrown weapon attack, a second target in Range 4 of the first takes damage equal to your Sneak attack die.</p><hr><p><em>[A] The INT/Safe Rest uses are a counter on this feature, tracked on the sheet (click the counter to correct mistakes).</em></p><p><em>[A] After a thrown weapon attack hits (<strong>Thrown attack?</strong> ticked in its dialog), a prompt asks for the second target — creatures within Range 4 of the first are listed first — and this feature rolls one Sneak Attack die against it: its own damage card with an Apply button, spending a use (the card has an Undo button). Using the feature from the sheet does the same against your current target.</em></p><p><em>[A] The die is one die of your current Sneak Attack size (d8 at level 7, d10 at 9, d12 at 11, d20 from 15).</em></p>",
